      "writtenOn": "2017-02-03T23:24:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is assuming that you\u0027re using the standard context cancellation function, which only does something once, so calling it twice is useless. The second signal is triggering a panic, which is quickly fatal. I made a longer comment on SetupSignals above to describe this.\n\nDoing something better here would be nice, this was basically the minimum necessary. Using a timeout instead of waiting for another signal may be a good idea. It would be nice if we the first kill didn\u0027t do anything to print out more about what didn\u0027t die. Same thing with the first alarm signal -- do some debug prints, then kill things.",
